---
applyTo: "src/content/post/**"
---
## Voice
Follow `.github/instructions/voice.instructions.md` for tone, phrasing, openings, closings and the words to avoid. This file covers what's specific to blog posts.

## Pick the right shape
Don't force every post into the same structure. Choose the archetype that fits:

- **Quick link / news post.** One to three paragraphs, no headings. Say what it is, why you care and where to find it. Add a wry closing line if one comes naturally.
- **Maker / build log.** Open with the story or the itch you were scratching. Then use descriptive `##` headings for each stage, numbered steps where order matters, and a parts list with links. Be honest about what went wrong and finish with what's next. Example: `src/content/post/2026/11/porting-doom-to-the-universe-badge-with-copilot.mdx`
- **Reflection / opinion.** Write a narrative with a few headings that carry the argument. Use a single bold pull-quote for the key idea, and real numbers rather than adjectives. Example: `src/content/post/2026/11/building-with-heart-in-the-age-of-ai.mdx`

Use code blocks, images, embeds and lists only where they help the reader.

## Structure & Format
- **Path**: `src/content/post/yyyy/mm/descriptive-filename.md` (or `.mdx` when components are needed)
- **Images**: `/images/post/yyyy/mm/filename.jpg`. Use `/images/image-placeholder.png` if none is provided.
- **Links**: link generously and in context. Link products, projects, people, earlier posts and talks.
- **Title**: plain and descriptive, or playful when the post is ("Copilot Hacked my Furby!"). Use title case. Avoid clickbait.
- **Description**: one short sentence (two at most) in Martin's voice, with a hook that makes you want to read the post. Don't list everything the post covers. It is not an SEO keyword list.

## Categories & Tags
Prefer existing categories (most used first):
`web` `technology` `programming` `maker` `personal` `dotnet` `gadgets` `podcast` `books` `git` `github` `ai` `community` `tfs`

Tags are free-form, lowercase and hyphenated (e.g. `github-copilot`, `open-source`).

## Publishing
There are no drafts. A post goes live when its PR is merged. If `date` is in the future, the post stays out of the site, RSS and search until that time passes and the next scheduled build (06:07 and 18:07 UTC) picks it up.

## Frontmatter Template
```yaml
---
title: "Descriptive Title"
date: 2026-11-12T10:00:00.000Z
images: ["/images/post/2026/11/filename.jpg"]
author: "Martin Woodward"
description: "One or two sentences, in Martin's voice."
categories: ["maker", "github"]
tags: ["relevant", "tags"]
type: "regular"
---
```

## PR Guidelines
- Only modify the post file and its images. Never touch `package-lock.json` or config files.
- Never invent personal anecdotes, quotes or facts. Leave `TODO(Martin):` placeholders for anything only Martin can supply.
